From 9b734b920bd3f93b5f2cfd8cffcf86bd9bf3b02c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cliffhall <cliff@futurescale.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:58:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix: resolve options before item-add; measure the
 board-ops hand-off

Address the four "previously missed" findings in Copilot's second
review round on #4899:

- board-ops add-card resolves both option ids before item-add, so a
  failed lookup or a renamed option never leaves a card with no Status
  or Priority.
- issue-create's board duplicate check refuses an incomplete listing
  (length vs totalCount), as board-ops requires of whole-board dumps.
- issue-create's create command takes the type and scope labels as
  placeholders from step 1 instead of a hard-coded bug/server-filesystem.
- issue-create now points at board-ops imperatively, at the top and at
  step 5, and board-ops carries an issue-create -> board-ops chain case
  (100% at RUNS=5; the whole suite stays at 14/14 first-move cases).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: cliffhall <cliff@futurescale.com>
